{"name":"Violet Sweet Pea","hex":"#c7c5dc","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"violet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata;  similar-looking plants and flowers.","A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a violet colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet"},{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"pea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Peranakan Indonesian."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of certain plants of the family Fabaceae: Pisum sativum and others.","A plant, Pisum sativum, member of the legume (Fabaceae) family."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet pea","blocks":[{"text":"The sweet pea, Lathyrus odoratus, is a flowering plant in the genus Lathyrus in the family Fabaceae (legumes), native to Sicily, southern Italy and the Aegean Islands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Sweet_Pea-7.jpg/330px-Sweet_Pea-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_pea","wikidata":"Q163944"},{"title":"Pea","blocks":[{"text":"Pea is a pulse or fodder crop, but the word often refers to the seed or sometimes the pod of this flowering plant species. Peas are eaten as a vegetable. The pea is native to the Mediterranean region and southwest Asia, and cultivated nearly worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Doperwt_rijserwt_peulen_Pisum_sativum.jpg/330px-Doperwt_rijserwt_peulen_Pisum_sativum.jpg?ut